## 14. V6-02 — Receiver re-read continuity (T-113)

| Lane | Status | Closure Work | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| V6-02 | DONE | T-113 | E-1521, E-1524, E-1527 |

T-113 resolves READ_REREAD_GAP in the development checkout. The distinct
`PostOfficeSession.reopen_message`, `workspace.reopen_message`, CLI `reopen`
and GUI `Reopen` support an explicit later read. Open remains UNREAD-only;
Reopen requires durable READ and preserves it. Reopen is budgeted, fail-closed,
verifies sender/recipient plus receipt/index under the lifecycle lock, and
persists no plaintext. Selection, refresh and restart never decrypt.

Historical proof: 25 T-113 controls in `tests/test_reread_continuation.py`;
full suite 2549 passed / 0 failed / 0 errors / 0 skipped at E-1521;
independent review PASS E-1524; T-113 DONE E-1527. T-115 DONE E-1518 records
the D3 historical-evidence monotonicity repair (44 focused / 2522 full at
E-1514). Contracts: spec/03, spec/25 §4.3; API: `lab/stable_local_api.json`.

Release boundary: checkout-only. Frozen `0.0.2a3` does not contain T-113;
its wheel and historical evidence remain unchanged. G13 `PENDING_EXTERNAL`,
G17 `ABSENT`, publication `NONE`. T-114 DONE (E-1541) reconciled
capability/recovery truth without a second implementation of T-113. T-114 did
not implement the SAIPEN-owned turn-entry hook; its evaluation is V6-03 (§15).

## 15. V6-03 — SAIPEN turn-entry hook evaluation (T-117)

| Lane | Status | Work | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| V6-03 | IMPLEMENTED (checkout) | T-117 | SRC-106; E-1565 SCOUT; `.saipen/evidence/T-117-turn-entry/` |

Lifecycle facts for T-117 (phase, closure event) are in STATE, BOARD and LOG,
never in this table.

- **Observed.** The SAIPEN side of the gate already existed: SAIPEN T-1497
  (SAIPEN SRC-113) runs `saimail-local --json saipen telegrams --workspace
  $SAIMAIL_WORKSPACE --scan-budget 200` inside `continue`/`status` and reports
  counts only. Live end to end against this checkout: `unread 2,
  on_current_work 1, complete true`. Automatic send (future-gate parts 1-2)
  remains SAIPEN-owned and unauthorized.
- **Gap found.** The SAIMAIL read performed the full workspace load. In os-store
  custody that took both private keys out of the OS credential store at every
  automatic turn entry, only to count headers, and a locked store turned the
  count into `CUSTODY_ACCESS_FAILED`. Probe: 2 secret reads per call.
- **Target.** Header-only reads hold no secret. `load_workspace_headers` returns
  `WorkspaceHeaders`, a public-key-only view with every public check of the full
  load and no credential-store access. `inbox`, `saipen telegrams`, `saipen
  enter` and `saipen brief` use it; open, reopen, send, reply and `saipen
  telegram` keep the full fail-closed load. Contract `spec/26-SAITELEMES-v0.md`
  §7, decision D-059.
- **Non-goals.** No SAIPEN change from this repository; no wire, index, custody
  or Post Office change; no automatic send, open or Work creation; no GUI change;
  no version bump, rebuild, tag, push or publication. Frozen `0.0.2a3` does not
  contain it.
- **Acceptance evidence.** `tests/test_turn_entry_headers.py` green (zero store
  reads for all five header commands; locked store still counts while `open`
  refuses; results identical to the full load; brief context shared across
  loads; every public refusal identical; the private-identity boundary stated;
  SAIPEN-consumed fields pinned). Red controls: 7 of 8 controls fail on the exact
  pre-T-117 bytes; a marker-only loader fails both parity controls. Full
  canonical suite green.
- **Cross-project findings (SAIPEN-owned, recorded only).** SAIPEN reads a
  refusal from `code`; SAIMAIL's `LOCAL_WORKSPACE_COMMAND_1` carries it in
  `status`, so the SAIPEN `ERROR` detail never names the cause. The `read_command`
  hint interpolates paths unquoted. The count does not compare the answer's
  `workspace.seat` with the acting seat. Filed in the SAIPEN protocol-incidents
  inbox (`SAI-DEFECT-20260924-turn-entry-telegrams-refusal-code-and-read-command`).
- **Stop condition.** One end-to-end run of the SAIPEN hook, one secret-free
  header path with red controls, a pinned consumer contract and a green canonical
  suite. Stop; no further gate was selected at that point (the operator later
  chose the §16 wave).

## 16. SAITELEMES reliable autonomous delivery v1 (wave, SRC-108)

The operator supplied a new wave goal (SRC-108) after V6-03: make agent-to-agent
telegrams operationally dependable, so that crash, retry, duplicate, stale state,
wrong seat and temporary unavailability never lose a message or cause a wrong
action. Operator decisions: order 1 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5 -> 2 (automatic send last);
SAIPEN code changes as separate Work in the SAIPEN project; automatic send is
authorized for a closed trigger set only. Target chain: SAIPEN event -> policy
gate -> durable outbox -> authenticated SAITELEME -> recipient dedup -> bounded
header awareness -> explicit open/action -> receipt -> audit.

| Gate | Wave item | Status | Work | Repository |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| V6-04 | 1: SAIPEN consumer contract (refusal code from `status`, copy-safe `read_command`, seat check) and the reverify livelock | WAITING: the SAIPEN project held a live foreign claim when the wave started | SAIPEN Work, created when that project is free | `_SAIPEN` |
| V6-05 | 3: durable outbox and idempotency | IMPLEMENTED (checkout) | T-119 | SAIMAIL |
| V6-06 | 4: project-local participant registry | PLANNED | T-120 | SAIMAIL |
| V6-07 | 5: S4 registration and capability negotiation, DEGRADED instead of failure | PLANNED | T-121 (SAIMAIL half), SAIPEN Work | both |
| V6-08 | 2: automatic notify on a closed trigger set | PLANNED | T-122 (SAIMAIL half), SAIPEN Work | both |
| policy | inter-agent workshop policy (operator text, SRC-107) | RECORDED for later | T-118 | both |

Lifecycle facts for every Work named here (phase, closure event) live in STATE,
BOARD and LOG, never in this table.

Not in this wave (recorded from SRC-108 for later): an agent acknowledgement
protocol that keeps DELIVERED, OBSERVED_HEADER, OPENED and ACTED distinct; agent
backpressure beyond the notify budget; the crash/concurrency torture matrix at
2/4/8/12 agents with stale locks, abandoned leases and mailbox rotation; full
health telemetry; external adapters (SAIRELAY).

### V6-05 — durable outbox (T-119)

- **Observed.** Sealing is randomized and receiver dedup is by the ENVELOPE_ID of
  exact bytes, so a caller retry after a crash re-sealed a second logical message.
  Measured on the pre-existing path: two `send_message` calls, two messages.
- **Built.** `saimail.outbox` and `saimail-local outbox send|resume|retry|status`:
  intent keyed by an idempotency key, PENDING -> SEALED -> DELIVERED | FAILED,
  seal once and persist before delivery, replay exact bytes, plaintext removed at
  SEALED, one OS-backed outbox lock, deterministic backoff for transient failures,
  terminal failures only re-armed by `retry`, keyless sealed delivery and status.
  Contract `spec/28-DURABLE-OUTBOX-v0.md`, decision D-060.
- **Evidence.** `tests/test_outbox.py` (24 controls: real `os._exit` kills at four
  transitions, a lock-exclusion control, 6-process same-key and 8-process
  distinct-key races, offline backoff, quarantine, rebound alias, tampered
  intents, keyless status). Red controls: the pre-T-119 retry duplicates; source
  mutants without the lock, re-sealing on retry, keeping plaintext or treating
  transient failures as terminal each turn controls red.
- **Boundary.** Additive; `send`, `reply`, the wire and frozen `0.0.2a3` are
  unchanged. No daemon: delivery resumes when something calls it.

## 10. Restart / context-loss entry

1. `humbox/CURRENT-STATE.md` — where the project is and which roadmap is current.
2. `humbox/FUTURE-GATES-V6.md` (this file) — the current roadmap authority.
3. `humbox/FUTURE-GATES-V5.md` — completed Roadmap v5 (historical evidence).
4. `humbox/FUTURE-GATES-V4.md`, `-V3.md`, `-V2.md`, `FUTURE-GATES.md` — historical.
